From: Ian Clarke <sanity@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Mar 2026 16:36:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 49/69] fix(ui): replace onscroll with IntersectionObserver to
 eliminate scroll jank (#154)

* fix(ui): replace onscroll with IntersectionObserver to eliminate scroll jank

Replace the per-scroll-event DOM queries (scrollTop/clientHeight/scrollHeight)
with an IntersectionObserver on a sentinel div at the bottom of the chat
container. The observer fires only on intersection changes, eliminating
all JavaScript work during normal scrolling.

Closes #151

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix: remove unnecessary relative class from scroll container

Code-first review finding: the `relative` class on the scroll container
was not needed for IntersectionObserver functionality and was adding
unnecessary positioning context.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix: use rootMargin instead of 100px sentinel, fix misleading comment

Address skeptical review findings:
- Use rootMargin "0px 0px 100px 0px" with a 1px sentinel instead of a
  100px-tall div, eliminating extra scrollable whitespace
- Fix misleading comment about observer cleanup to accurately document
  that it relies on Conversation being mounted once (CSS show/hide)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

